    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14757" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dorsŭālis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		dorsum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>on the back</i>, <i>dorsal</i> (post-class): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">notae equi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 11, p. 266, 32</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crustae ferarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 22, 15</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">and, pinnae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 12</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dorsualia</span></b> , ium, n.,
				<i>a cover for the back</i> of beasts, Trebell.
			Gallien. 8.</div>
